Q: Terraform errors with &quot;provider_config is not a supported block&quot; for databricks_rfa_access_request_destinations A: <p>According to the schema for the <code>databricks_rfa_access_request_destinations</code> resource type (returned as part of the <code>terraform providers schema -json</code> output), <code>provider_config</code> is defined as being a direct argument rather than a nested block type, so you need to use argument syntax instead of block syntax:</p>
<pre><code>  provider_config = {  
    workspace_id = data.databricks_mws_workspaces.all.ids[var.catalogs[each.value.name].workspace_name]
  }  
</code></pre>
